-- title:
--   Explicit two-sided quasi-inverse of σ - r on L⊗_K A
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a finite-dimensional Galois extension of $K$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$, and assume that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$, so that the Galois group is cyclic and generated by $\sigma$. Let $A$ be a commutative $K$-algebra and put $E = L \otimes_K A$; for a $K$-automorphism $g$ of $L$ write $g_E = g \otimes \mathrm{id}_A$ for the ring endomorphism `sigmaTensor` of $E$ obtained by tensoring $g$ with the identity of $A$. Let $r, y \in E$, set $\ell = \dim_K L$, write $N(r) \in A$ for the norm `Algebra.norm A r` of $r$ for the $A$-algebra $E$, and put $$M_r(y) = \sum_{j < \ell} \Big( \prod_{i < j} (\sigma^{-1}_E)^{i+1}(r) \Big) \cdot (\sigma^{-1}_E)^{j+1}(y),$$ the iterates being those of the map attached to $\sigma^{-1}$. Then both $$\sigma_E\big(M_r(y)\big) - r\,M_r(y) = (1 - N(r))\,y \quad\text{and}\quad M_r\big(\sigma_E(y) - r\,y\big) = (1 - N(r))\,y$$ hold in $E$, where $1 - N(r) \in A$ acts through the structure map $A \to E$.
--
--   The displayed sum $M_r$ is the twisted resolvent of the operator $y \mapsto \sigma_E(y) - r y$ on $E = L \otimes_K A$, and the two identities say that it is a two-sided quasi-inverse with factor $1 - N(r)$; this is the computation underlying the classical Hilbert 90 / cyclic-algebra argument in the form used for twisted orbital integrals. It is invoked in the construction of explicit continuous linear equivalences computing archimedean evaluations of the resolvent at real and complex places.
